1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,031
Standard form with powers of ten. Among all the

2
00:00:03,031 --> 00:00:05,439
exponent laws, this one is the most useful in

3
00:00:05,439 --> 00:00:08,520
science: it writes very large and very small numbers

4
00:00:08,520 --> 00:00:13,200
compactly. Move the decimal point, count the places, and

5
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:14,811
write the power of ten.

6
00:00:15,327 --> 00:00:18,387
Standard form begins with two extremes. The Sun is

7
00:00:18,387 --> 00:00:21,367
about three hundred million metres away. A wire inside

8
00:00:21,367 --> 00:00:24,593
a computer chip is about zero point zero zero

9
00:00:24,593 --> 00:00:28,087
zero zero zero three metres across. Powers of ten

10
00:00:28,087 --> 00:00:30,980
write both: three times ten to the power eight,

11
00:00:30,980 --> 00:00:34,418
and three times ten to the power minus six.

12
00:00:35,047 --> 00:00:36,898
Powers of ten are really a scale. Ten to

13
00:00:36,898 --> 00:00:39,967
the power zero is one, in the middle. To

14
00:00:39,967 --> 00:00:43,787
the right the numbers grow: ten, one hundred, one

15
00:00:43,787 --> 00:00:47,170
thousand. To the left they shrink below one: one

16
00:00:47,170 --> 00:00:51,987
tenth, one hundredth, one thousandth. So a positive exponent

17
00:00:51,987 --> 00:00:55,315
means a large scale, and a negative exponent means

18
00:00:55,315 --> 00:00:56,418
a small scale.

19
00:00:57,067 --> 00:00:59,455
Now convert a large number: three hundred million. The

20
00:00:59,455 --> 00:01:02,607
decimal point sits at the right-hand end. Move it

21
00:01:02,607 --> 00:01:06,207
left, one place at a time, until a single

22
00:01:06,207 --> 00:01:08,487
non-zero digit stands in front of it: that is

23
00:01:08,487 --> 00:01:13,136
eight places. So three hundred million is three times

24
00:01:13,136 --> 00:01:14,978
ten to the power eight.

25
00:01:15,833 --> 00:01:19,147
Here is a second large number: six thousand and

26
00:01:19,147 --> 00:01:23,824
twenty million. Again the decimal point begins at the

27
00:01:23,824 --> 00:01:26,422
right-hand end. Move it left until only one non-zero

28
00:01:26,422 --> 00:01:30,533
digit stands in front: one, two, three, four, five,

29
00:01:30,533 --> 00:01:34,939
six, seven, eight, nine places. The digits we keep

30
00:01:34,939 --> 00:01:37,973
are six, zero, two. So the number is six

31
00:01:37,973 --> 00:01:40,864
point zero two times ten to the power nine.

32
00:01:41,414 --> 00:01:44,334
Now a very small number: the wire inside a

33
00:01:44,334 --> 00:01:47,746
chip is zero point zero zero zero zero zero

34
00:01:47,746 --> 00:01:51,361
three metres across. This time the decimal point starts

35
00:01:51,361 --> 00:01:54,569
at the left. Move it right until only one

36
00:01:54,569 --> 00:01:57,100
non-zero digit stands in front: that is six places,

37
00:01:57,100 --> 00:02:01,266
and the digit is three. Because we moved right,

38
00:02:01,266 --> 00:02:05,168
into a number that was smaller than one, the

39
00:02:05,168 --> 00:02:11,085
exponent is negative: three times ten to the power minus six.

40
00:02:11,851 --> 00:02:15,096
A plant cell is even more interesting: it is

41
00:02:15,096 --> 00:02:17,807
zero point zero zero zero zero one two seven

42
00:02:17,807 --> 00:02:21,381
five metres across. The significant digits are one, two,

43
00:02:21,381 --> 00:02:24,471
seven and five, and they do not change. Move

44
00:02:24,471 --> 00:02:27,311
the decimal point right: one, two, three, four, five

45
00:02:27,311 --> 00:02:30,000
places. So the standard form is one point two

46
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:32,620
seven five times ten to the power minus five.

47
00:02:32,620 --> 00:02:36,168
The quantity is the same; only the way we

48
00:02:36,168 --> 00:02:37,902
write it has changed.

49
00:02:38,541 --> 00:02:42,801
Now the other direction: from standard form back to

50
00:02:42,801 --> 00:02:45,961
usual form. Four point six seven times ten to

51
00:02:45,961 --> 00:02:49,106
the power four: the exponent is positive, so the

52
00:02:49,106 --> 00:02:53,123
decimal point moves right four places, giving forty six

53
00:02:53,123 --> 00:02:55,751
thousand seven hundred. Three point zero two times ten

54
00:02:55,751 --> 00:02:59,621
to the power minus six: the exponent is negative,

55
00:02:59,621 --> 00:03:02,369
so the decimal point moves left six places, giving

56
00:03:02,369 --> 00:03:04,904
zero point zero zero zero zero zero three zero

57
00:03:04,904 --> 00:03:07,911
two. These directions are for going back to usual

58
00:03:07,911 --> 00:03:11,572
form; making standard form moves the decimal the other way.

59
00:03:12,326 --> 00:03:15,510
Here is the complete map. A large number in

60
00:03:15,510 --> 00:03:17,932
usual form moves its decimal point left and takes

61
00:03:17,932 --> 00:03:22,392
a positive exponent. A small number moves its decimal

62
00:03:22,392 --> 00:03:26,532
point right and takes a negative exponent. Coming back

63
00:03:26,532 --> 00:03:30,774
from standard form the movements reverse: a positive exponent

64
00:03:30,774 --> 00:03:34,308
moves the decimal right, and a negative exponent moves

65
00:03:34,308 --> 00:03:36,757
it left. Always ask which direction you are converting.

66
00:03:37,247 --> 00:03:41,302
Your turn. Three conversions. Write zero point zero zero

67
00:03:41,302 --> 00:03:44,593
zero zero four five six in standard form. Write

68
00:03:44,593 --> 00:03:48,222
six thousand and twenty million in standard form. And

69
00:03:48,222 --> 00:03:51,347
write five point eight times ten to the power

70
00:03:51,347 --> 00:03:52,958
seven in usual form.

71
00:04:03,978 --> 00:04:07,098
For the first, the decimal moves right five places,

72
00:04:07,098 --> 00:04:09,150
so it is four point five six times ten

73
00:04:09,150 --> 00:04:12,478
to the power minus five. For the second, the

74
00:04:12,478 --> 00:04:15,599
decimal moves left nine places: six point zero two

75
00:04:15,599 --> 00:04:18,138
times ten to the power nine. And for the

76
00:04:18,138 --> 00:04:22,114
third the exponent is positive seven, so the decimal

77
00:04:22,114 --> 00:04:24,889
moves right seven places: fifty eight million.

78
00:04:25,534 --> 00:04:27,854
One last look at the whole idea. Move the

79
00:04:27,854 --> 00:04:31,034
decimal point, count the places, choose the sign, and

80
00:04:31,034 --> 00:04:34,039
write times ten to the power: three hundred million

81
00:04:34,039 --> 00:04:36,723
is three times ten to the power eight. And

82
00:04:36,723 --> 00:04:39,264
zero point zero zero zero zero zero three is

83
00:04:39,264 --> 00:04:42,874
three times ten to the power minus six. Powers

84
00:04:42,874 --> 00:04:44,544
of ten let us write the very large and

85
00:04:44,544 --> 00:04:47,784
the very small compactly. Thank you for watching the

86
00:04:47,784 --> 00:04:50,425
chapter, and see you in the next lesson.
